# University paperwork — deliberately untracked.
# The signed proposal carries handwritten signatures, a student ID and a university
# email. This repository is public, so those must never reach history: a leak here
# cannot be undone by a later delete. The files stay on disk in admin/, untracked.
#
# Both rules on purpose. admin/ covers the documents where they live; the blanket
# extension rules are the net for a document that lands anywhere else — the project
# root is where these files sat until 2026-07-30, so it is the likely accident.
# If a real PDF figure ever needs tracking, negate it explicitly below rather than
# widening the rule — `git add -f` also works.
admin/
*.pdf
*.docx
*.pptx

# The thesis figures, one file each rather than a glob, so a stray document dropped
# into figures/ is still caught. Generated by experiments/thesis_figures.py; their
# only metadata is Matplotlib's Creator/Producer.
!docs/thesis/latex/figures/comparison-diurnal.pdf
!docs/thesis/latex/figures/comparison-ramp.pdf
!docs/thesis/latex/figures/comparison-spike.pdf
!docs/thesis/latex/figures/comparison-bursty.pdf
!docs/thesis/latex/figures/ablation-spike.pdf

# Python (simulator)
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
*.pyc

# Go
bin/
*.test
*.out

# Experiment output — raw series are regenerated by experiments/run.sh.
# Note: sim/results/*.png IS tracked; those are the thesis fallback figures.
experiments/results/raw/

# Sweep console logs. Kept on disk next to the results because a multi-hour
# unattended sweep dies for reasons that only appear here (a dropped port-forward,
# Docker Desktop going away), but they are console noise, not evidence — the
# evidence is run.json.
experiments/results/logs/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Defense deck build products — docs/defense/build.sh regenerates both from the thesis
# figures and slides.js, the same way the thesis PDF is left untracked.
docs/defense/img/
